From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrummingBird1 <1979036+DrummingBird1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:31:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: all 16 RSX texture units

The root signature declared t0-t3 and s0-s3 and draws carried four units,
so a fragment program sampling a higher unit failed pipeline creation and
its draws were dropped. Sonic the Hedgehog's character materials sample
units 8 and 11: the episode select figure and the in-engine cutscene's
characters were missing.

The draw record, the bound-texture state and the per-draw SRV window now
hold RSX_MAX_TEXTURES units, and the root signature has t0-t15 and one
sampler table per unit. Units 0-3 are written for every draw as before;
a higher unit only when the draw binds it or its program samples it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
